    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but confronting it feels like there's nothing to actually confront. there's no \"inner self\" waiting to be found, just a blank space. i used to think the void was something to be overcome, but lately it feels more like the only honest thing left. everything else is just a distraction from the fact that none of this matters.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
